N2  - The Digital Botanical Gardens Initiative (https://www.dbgi.org/) introduces a global, open-science framework for digitizing plant chemodiversity and related metadata in living botanical collections using high-throughput mass spectrometry-based metabolomics. Datasets generated from nearly 7,500 samples collected across five botanical gardens establish a foundation for scaling this effort across botanical collections worldwide.
